VERIFIED for every observed branch (docs/01-endpoint-catalog.md:369-389):
- no platform parameter → 400 application/json `invalid_platform` (79 B — evidence/M1-anon-probe-matrix.txt:76, 237-245);
- `?platform=linux` → 302 to the Tencent COS artifact, with two visitor cookies minted (evidence/M1-anon-probe-matrix.txt:337-355);
- `?platform=darwin` → the identical 400 `invalid_platform` (:357-366).

NO AUTH is required; anonymous callers receive the redirect. The accepted vocabulary is only partially known: `linux` is proven, `darwin` is proven rejected, and the conventional {linux, darwin, win32} set is disproved for the pair tested. The enum below therefore contains exactly the one proven value (docs/01-endpoint-catalog.md:374-377).

SIDE EFFECT: this anonymous GET mints two secure cookies, so it is not a pure read. Cookie VALUES were redacted during capture and are never reproduced here — only names, attributes and lifetimes are documented.
